    description: "Found by the 2026-11-24 docstring staleness audit (dev 7e204b35b): a reviewer flagged it and a default-REJECT verifier re-reproduced it on a fixture of its own (reports under ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/staleness_audit_11242026/review and verify). Corpus impact not measured. The index-assignment handler takes the first identifier child of the index_expression (rust_def_use.py:260-263); when the base is a field_expression the first identifier child is the index. `self.data[i] = v;` gives defines [i], uses [self, i, v], which kills the reaching definition of i; `data[i] = v;` correctly defines data. The module docstring says an index write is a mutation of the indexed value (rust_def_use.py:13). Found by the blind re-review b01; re-run by the orchestrator."  # 27d6
